cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "erc-ai-feedback: a prompt + rubric for AI triage of ERC StG/CoG drafts"
message: >-
  If this tool informs a teaching, workshop, or research process you
  publish about, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Tomáš
    family-names: Havránek
    affiliation: Charles University, Prague
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3158-2539"
repository-code: "https://github.com/tjhavranek/erc-ai-feedback"
url: "https://github.com/tjhavranek/erc-ai-feedback"
abstract: >-
  A small package consisting of a locked ERC Starting / Consolidator
  Grant evaluation rubric (verbatim sub-questions from the ERC Guide
  for Peer Reviewers v6.0) and a single self-contained AI prompt that
  loads the rubric, applies structural score caps, and enforces an
  evidence-grounded, no-sycophancy critique register. Intended to
  triage routine issues in proposal drafts so human reviewers can
  focus on the harder problems only experienced reviewers can flag.
  Not a substitute for human peer review or ERC support groups.
keywords:
